model_answer_en:
Definition
An array is a fixed-size collection of elements of the same data type stored in contiguous memory and accessed by an index (a[0] … a[n-1]). A structure (struct) is a user-defined type that groups members of different data types under one name; each member is accessed by name with the dot operator (s.roll).

Differences
| Point | Array | Structure |
|---|---|---|
| Element type | all elements of one type | members may be of different types |
| Access | by index: marks[2] | by member name: s.cgpa |
| Declaration | int marks[3]; | struct Student { int roll; char name[20]; float cgpa; }; |
| Kind of type | derived type; no new type name | user-defined type; struct Student can declare many variables |
| Memory | n × sizeof(element), no gaps | sum of members plus possible padding for alignment |
| Name in expressions | decays to a pointer to element 0 | does not decay; a struct is a value |
| Assignment and passing | cannot assign a = b; passed to a function as an address | s1 = s2 copies all members; passed to a function by value (a copy) |
| Typical use | a list of marks, prices, readings | one record: a student, an account, an employee |

Example
#include <stdio.h>

struct Student {            /* different types under one name */
    int roll;
    char name[20];
    float cgpa;
};

int main(void) {
    int marks[3] = {78, 85, 92};                  /* same type, by index */
    struct Student s = {101, "Rahim", 3.75f};     /* mixed types, by name */

    printf("%d %d\n", marks[0], marks[2]);
    printf("%d %s %.2f\n", s.roll, s.name, s.cgpa);
    return 0;
}

Output:
78 92
101 Rahim 3.75

The two are often combined: struct Student list[50]; is an array of structures (one record per student), and char name[20] is an array inside a structure.

Advantages and limitations
• An array gives O(1) access by position and easy looping, but every element must have the same type and the size is fixed at compile time.
• A structure keeps related data of different types together, making records readable and easy to pass around, but it cannot be indexed and padding may waste a few bytes.

model_answer_bn:
সংজ্ঞা
Array হলো একই data type-এর নির্দিষ্ট সংখ্যক element-এর সংগ্রহ, যা পাশাপাশি (contiguous) memory-তে থাকে এবং index দিয়ে ব্যবহার করা হয় (a[0] … a[n-1])। Structure (struct) হলো user-defined type, যা ভিন্ন ভিন্ন data type-এর member-কে একটি নামের অধীনে রাখে; প্রতিটি member নাম ধরে dot operator দিয়ে ব্যবহার করা হয় (s.roll)।

পার্থক্য
| বিষয় | Array | Structure |
|---|---|---|
| Element-এর type | সব element একই type | member ভিন্ন type-এর হতে পারে |
| ব্যবহার | index দিয়ে: marks[2] | member-এর নাম দিয়ে: s.cgpa |
| Declaration | int marks[3]; | struct Student { int roll; char name[20]; float cgpa; }; |
| Type-এর ধরন | derived type; নতুন type নাম নেই | user-defined type; struct Student দিয়ে অনেক variable declare করা যায় |
| Memory | n × sizeof(element), ফাঁক নেই | member-গুলোর যোগফল, alignment-এর জন্য padding থাকতে পারে |
| Expression-এ নাম | element 0-এর pointer-এ decay হয় | decay হয় না; struct একটি মান |
| Assignment ও pass | a = b লেখা যায় না; function-এ address হিসেবে যায় | s1 = s2 সব member copy করে; function-এ by value (copy) যায় |
| সাধারণ ব্যবহার | নম্বর, দাম, reading-এর তালিকা | একটি record: ছাত্র, হিসাব, কর্মচারী |

উদাহরণ
