stem_en:
On a 64-bit (x86-64) compiler, find sizeof for each declaration below, showing the offset of every member, and rewrite R so that it uses the least memory:
struct A { char c; int i; char d; };
struct R { char c; double d; int i; };
union U { char c[5]; int i; };
struct Bits { unsigned a : 3; unsigned b : 4; unsigned c : 1; };

stem_bn:
64-bit (x86-64) compiler-এ নিচের প্রতিটি declaration-এর sizeof বের করুন, প্রতিটি member-এর offset দেখিয়ে, এবং R-কে এমনভাবে আবার লিখুন যাতে সবচেয়ে কম memory লাগে:
struct A { char c; int i; char d; };
struct R { char c; double d; int i; };
union U { char c[5]; int i; };
struct Bits { unsigned a : 3; unsigned b : 4; unsigned c : 1; };

model_answer_en:
Assumptions (x86-64): char 1, int and unsigned 4, double 8 bytes, each aligned to its size; a member starts at a multiple of its alignment and the total is rounded up to the largest alignment.

struct A:
| Member | Offset | Note |
|---|---|---|
| c | 0 | |
| i | 4 | 3 padding bytes (1–3) |
| d | 8 | |
End 9 → rounded to a multiple of 4 → sizeof(A) = 12.

struct R:
| Member | Offset | Note |
|---|---|---|
| c | 0 | |
| d | 8 | 7 padding bytes (1–7) |
| i | 16 | |
End 20 → rounded to a multiple of 8 → sizeof(R) = 24.

union U: all members at offset 0; largest c = 5 bytes; alignment 4 (int) → sizeof(U) = 8.

struct Bits: a, b and c need 3 + 4 + 1 = 8 bits, packed into one unsigned int → sizeof(Bits) = 4.

Reordered R (largest alignment first):
struct R2 { double d; int i; char c; };
d 0–7, i 8–11, c 12, end 13 → rounded to 16. sizeof(R2) = 16, saving 8 bytes per record (80 KB for 10,000 records).

#include <stdio.h>
#include <stddef.h>
struct A { char c; int i; char d; };
struct R { char c; double d; int i; };
struct R2 { double d; int i; char c; };
union U { char c[5]; int i; };
struct Bits { unsigned a : 3; unsigned b : 4; unsigned c : 1; };
int main(void) {
    printf("A=%zu R=%zu R2=%zu U=%zu Bits=%zu\n", sizeof(struct A), sizeof(struct R),
           sizeof(struct R2), sizeof(union U), sizeof(struct Bits));
    printf("offsets R: c=%zu d=%zu i=%zu\n", offsetof(struct R, c), offsetof(struct R, d), offsetof(struct R, i));
    return 0;
}
Output:
A=12 R=24 R2=16 U=8 Bits=4
offsets R: c=0 d=8 i=16

